WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.864
When the body was ready, the procession crossed the Nile to the western tombs, where the sun itself was believed to travel each night.

00:00:10.864 --> 00:00:20.756
Mourners followed the coffin, priests burned incense, and the tomb was sealed with food, furniture, and words of guidance.

00:00:20.756 --> 00:00:27.000
Thousands of years later, when we speak these names, the journey continues.

